sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "After release from the matrix, the number of motile Anthrobots rises along a sigmoidal curve over three weeks, with the largest change in motility on day 10, and this rise reflects a morphological reorganization that exposes cilia on the surface.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Anthrobot motility onset follows a sigmoidal time course peaking around day 10";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Gumuskaya G, Srivastava P, Cooper BG, Lesser H, Semegran B, Garnier S, Levin M, “Motile Living Biobots Self-Construct from Adult Human Somatic Progenitor Seed Cells”, Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany) (2024), doi:10.1002/advs.202303575; section “Results › Human Bronchial Epithelial Cells Self‐Construct into Multicellular Motile Living Architectures”. Scope: NHBE-derived Anthrobots in vitro, first 3 weeks after matrix dissolution"
}
